    "summary": "Virginia opossums are about the size of a small terrier, with a long, scaly, prehensile tail, a pointed snout, and dark, leathery ears. Their coat can appear grayish or darker depending on color phase, and their feet include an opposable, thumb-like big toe on the hind foot (without a claw). Females develop a pouch during breeding season for carrying young—one of the most distinctive life-history traits among mammals in the region.",
