    "ecologicalRole": "Armadillos are ecosystem “soil stirrers.” Their foraging disturbs the ground surface, which can help mix organic material into soil but may also be disruptive when concentrated. They also create burrows that other wildlife may use for shelter, and they serve as prey or scavenged carrion for larger animals.\n- Aerates and mixes soil through digging and foraging\n- Creates burrows that can become shelter for other species\n- Supports predator and scavenger food webs as prey/carcasses",
