    "ecologicalRole": "Texas Toads provide insect control and form part of the prey base for snakes, turtles, and other predators. Tadpoles contribute to nutrient cycling by feeding on algae and fine organic matter, helping convert temporary water resources into food for higher trophic levels.\n- Reduces insect numbers, especially after rains\n- Supports predators in riparian food webs\n- Tadpoles help process algae and organic matter in temporary pools",
