    "parkLocation": "Grass carp may be seen cruising along the edges of weedy ponds or lakes. They usually stay near their food, so places rich in submerged plants will hold them. Visitors might spot them at sunrise or sunset when fish sometimes come up shallow to feed on surface plants.",
