    "parkLocation": "In park lakes or ponds, look for crappie around fallen tree branches or artificial fish habitats. They school in deeper water during the day and come up in the shallows at night to feed. Anglers often find them by casting near docks or brush. Signs at fishing lakes may even show the special crappie-spot where underwater structures attract the schools.",
