    "parkLocation": "Spotted gar are often found in the shallow, marshy parts of park lakes or slow creek backwaters—places where cattails or lily pads grow. They can be seen near the surface or hiding below logs. During low water, they might strand in isolated pools. Signs in fish-focused parks may point out these “living fossils” in the fish community.",
