    "funFact": "- Despite their name, mosquitofish aren’t picky; they eat almost anything tiny they can fit in their mouths.  \n- They were introduced worldwide for mosquito control and are now one of the world’s most widespread freshwater fish (often unwittingly).  \n- In some parks, naturalists challenge visitors to spot a mosquitofish in a “mosquito habitat” as a fun game (they’re quite camouflaged until they dart)."
