    "funFact": "- Bowfin are sometimes called “mudfish” or “pond pike.” Their ability to breathe air lets them survive in muddy, low-water conditions.  \n- Early settlers believed bowfin broth had medicinal properties, leading to another nickname: “doctorfish.”  \n- They can ambush prey with a lightning strike, puffing out their gills to lure prey close — a hunting trick."
